e_spread":0.0,"_gate_roic_consistency":null,"_gp_roic_consistency":null,"_score_roic_consistency":0.0,"_gate_incr_roic":0.5716927077970331,"_gp_incr_roic":true,"_score_incr_roic":100.0,"_gate_margin_advantage":0.374508141735242,"_gp_margin_advantage":true,"_score_margin_advantage":100.0,"_gate_pool_share":null,"_gp_pool_share":null,"_score_pool_share":null,"_gate_rev_durability":null,"_gp_rev_durability":null,"_score_rev_durability":0.0,"_gate_fcf_durability":null,"_gp_fcf_durability":null,"_score_fcf_durability":0.0,"_gate_margins":-0.026083463743369263,"_gp_margins":false,"_score_margins":23.9,"_gate_fund_growth":null,"_gp_fund_growth":null,"_score_fund_growth":0.0,"_gate_shrhldr_yield":0.04620934443047862,"_gp_shrhldr_yield":true,"_score_shrhldr_yield":62.5,"_gate_share_shrink":-0.010980013817164846,"_gp_share_shrink":true,"_score_share_shrink":63.7,"_gate_sbc_dilution":0.051855646429139216,"_gp_sbc_dilution":false,"_score_sbc_dilution":13.6,"_gate_insider_own":0.06744,"_gp_insider_own":true,"_score_insider_own":45.0,"_gate_insider_buying":0.846,"_gp_insider_buying":true,"_score_insider_buying":84.6,"pf":[],"description_full":"Aurinia Pharmaceuticals Inc., a biopharmaceutical company, engages in delivering therapies to people living with autoimmune diseases with high unmet medical needs in the United States and Japan. The company offers LUPKYNIS (voclosporin), an oral therapy for the treatment of adult patients with active lupus nephritis. It also develops aritinercept, a dual inhibitor of B cell-activating factor and proliferation-inducing ligand for the potential treatment of autoimmune diseases. The company was founded in 1993 and is headquartered in Edmonton, Canada.","ceo_bio":"Mr. Kevin C. Tang | Chairman & CEO | Age 58","culture_narrative":"Employs approximately 128 people. Revenue per employee of $2.2M ranks in the top quartile among Healthcare peers, with revenue growing 41%/yr across its filed history. Each employee generates $1.1M of free cash flow annually. Stock-based compensation of $115K per employee reflects an ownership culture. Governance score flags low compensation governance risk (3/10).","financial_summary":["Aurinia Pharmaceuticals Inc is a mid-cap healthcare business with a $2.1B market cap on $283M of annual revenue.","The top line has compounded at +28% over the past three years, the kind of sustained demand persistence that marks a compounder. Operating margins are expanding by +49.0pp year-over-year, which is one of the strongest signals that the moat is deepening.","Returns on capital run at -29% against a 10% cost of capital, which means the business is destroying value with every dollar it reinvests.","The business throws off $135M in free cash flow \u2014 roughly 48 cents on every revenue dollar, which is the owner-earnings figure that actually belongs to shareholders. Cash conversion is thin at 0.47\u00d7, however, which raises the oldest question in analysis: are these earnings backed by cash?.","Accruals are elevated at +20.2% of assets, and Sloan showed firms building earnings through accruals rather than cash systematically underperform.","On the balance sheet, the balance sheet carries net cash, which is the gold standard: the business never has to make desperate decisions in a bad year, and interest coverage of 24\u00d7 is fortress-like.","Shareholder yield of 4.6% reflects a genuine commitment to returning capital rather than empire-building, and insiders hold 6.7% of the shares, and within its sector the business captures 4.2\u00d7 its fair share of profits, a structural advantage visible in the numbers."],"sector_headwinds":[{"text":"Accruals elevated at +20.2% of assets \u2014 Sloan showed firms building earnings through accruals rather than cash systematically underperform","sev":"red","cat":"quality"},{"text":"Above-average short interest at 5.9% of float","sev":"amber","cat":"sentiment"},{"text":"Patent cliffs, drug-pricing reform, and reimbursement pressure \u2014 a single regulatory change can reset the pricing power that justifies the multiple.","sev":"amber","cat":"thesis_risk"},{"text":"Clinical trial concentration risk \u2014 binary FDA outcomes on a lead asset can wipe out billions in market cap in a single session.","sev":"amber","cat":"thesis_risk"},{"text":"GLP-1 disruption across sub-sectors \u2014 weight-loss drugs are reshaping demand for orthopaedics, cardiovascular devices, and sleep-apnea treatments in ways not yet priced in.","sev":"amber","cat":"thesis_risk"}],"sector_tailwinds":["Operating margins 37% above sector median \u2014 the quantitative trace of pricing power","Trading at a 41% margin of safety to estimated fair value \u2014 a real cushion against errors in the estimate","Market is pricing in lower growth than the company has historically delivered","Valued at a 39% discount to sector median EV/EBITDA","Altman Z comfortably in the safe zone \u2014 a fortress balance sheet on this measure","Insiders are net buyers (85% buy ratio) \u2014 insiders sell for many reasons but buy for only one","Large open-market insider purchases (net $24.6M) \u2014 management putting its own capital behind the business","Healthcare sector showing strong relative momentum, outperforming the market by 13% over 3 months","Healthcare ETF in a sustained uptrend above its long-term average","Strong 6-month sector performance (30.7% return)"],"news_headlines":[{"title":"Aurinia Pharmaceuticals (NASDAQ:AUPH) & Cardio Diagnostics (NASDAQ:CDIO) Financial Analysis","source":"thelincolnianonline.com","link":"https://www.thelincolnianonline.com/2026/11/11/aurinia-pharmaceuticals-nasdaqauph-cardio-diagnostics-nasdaqcdio-financial-analysis.html","date":"2026-11-11","timestamp":1794406518.0,"origin":"tiingo","sentiment":0.909,"tier":0,"scope":"company","tags":[]},{"title":"Aurinia Pharmaceuticals (NASDAQ:AUPH) Stock Gets Downgrade from Wall Street Zen","source":"thelincolnianonline.com","link":"https://www.thelincolnianonline.com/2026/11/09/aurinia-p